    <node name="startup" channel="inline" format="text/cybol-path" model=".logic.startup"/>
-->

    <!-- TEST. Delete later! -->
    <node name="exit" channel="inline" format="live/exit" model=""/>

</node>

<!--
    This web application is an editor for cybol files.
    It is based on a tree for file selection and a table with four columns for editing.

    Start up this application:
    cd /home/cybop/tools
    ../src/controller/cyboi cybol-editor/run.cybol

    Open up a web browser and type in the following uri:
    http://localhost/?action=send-index

    Or some other port number for testing, since it does not require root access:
    http://localhost:1971/?action=send-index

    CAUTION! The programme needs to be shut down using the key combination ctrl+c!

    CAUTION! The reserved service ports 0..1023 can sometimes only be
    used when running the cybol application as "root" user (Administrator).
    In such cases, the cyboi interpreter might return an error message like:
    "TEST: startup bsd socket bind error EACCES: 13"

    The "nmap" tool may be used to find out about active service ports, e.g.:
    nmap localhost
-->
